			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839294">
									

<p>Seeking review of concept for an SCP article. Tried this out about nine years ago, did bad, and want to give it another go having read a lot more of the material and matured as a writer/person.</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up a lot of space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight:</strong> <strong>Yes</strong></p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror &amp; History</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard in-depth containment procedure, followed by a retrieval log and accompanied by a brief test log with two or three addenda related to the nature of the SCP. I don't want to perform anything out of the ordinary format-wise with it being my first entry, but a timeline of the SCP's apprehension by groups of interest may be relevant.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<p>A forest-spirit/lesser goddess of creation and fertility that asexually births creatures based<br />
upon what she consumes is captured by the Church of the Broken God, and turned into a weapon to convert organic material into inorganic material. They lose her, and she exchanges hands between organizations for hundreds of years before ending up in foundation custody totally unrecognizable to what she once was, with a sinister corruption of her godly ability.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<p>Following the first war of the Flesh, Cyrus the Great founded a covenant to search the world for a new means to defeat the Sarkic threat. This group set out, with generations passing before eventually finding a minor fertility goddess unique in her ability to produce life asexually and rapidly by consuming organic matter. They captured her, but became indoctrinated by the Church of the Broken God over time, and augmented her heavily. She would eventually escape with the aid of a man enamored with her, and sire a child with him, the location of which is unknown but she is believed to be endowed with the same ability. Over time different organizations got ahold of the spirit and altered her repeatedly to suit their needs or designs with her now bordering on unrecognizable as herself.</p>
<p>Her modern iteration is a mess of added mechanical and organic apertures both internal and external that have removed her god-like beauty to some extent. Her mistreatment by mankind has jaded her to the point of being predatory, and resulted in her fractured psyche turning to exploitation and predation of mankind through producing her unique offspring. Organic material she consumed is now converted into mechanically augmented horrors when she births them, and vice versa.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong></p>
<p>The concept of the perversion of sexuality, creation, and birth for the purpose of furthering an agenda is enticing and provocative. Taking an earthly minor-goddess of creation and weaponizing her between the Sarkites and Mekhanites and turning her into a cog in the war machine between them serves as a potent analogy for the corruption of life and nature to fit the destruction of it, while sympathizing the reader to a malignant goddess that was once benign and pure.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I believe I've thought this through reasonably well, but am making space to afford the word count. Some gaps in reasoning are apparent here that I don't have space to explain.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
