<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Hmm. I'm not sure how I feel about this as a SCP article: it feels like this really needs a like, historical observer who can tell this story from the outside as the various events happen; I could see perhaps it being a tale from the perspective of the SCP, or perhaps something like a Serpents Hand format?</p>
<p>Really my issue with this as a SCP is that 'the Foundation discovers the anomaly' feels too much like the end of the story than the start, and I'm kinda feeling like the history of the anomaly is the most interesting part? On the flip side, a deep, historical look at this could be very interesting if like, all the investigation is laid out; with the foundation assuming she's a new anomaly and then gradually piecing stuff together to the final ending where they discover who she was originally, y'know?</p>
<p>This ties into my concerns with:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>followed by a retrieval log and accompanied by a brief test log with two or three addenda related to the nature of the SCP.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not really sure what your addenda show, but I'm not convinced a test log would be that interesting here at all. I guess really what I want to know is how the narrative and the page layout tie together?</p>
</div>
